-- title:
--   Gauss units q/G and w_q(G) for the node coordinate G
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime, $A$ a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, and $\mathrm{red}\colon A \to k$ any ring homomorphism into an algebraically closed field $k$ of characteristic $q$; assume $q \ge 5$. Let $a \in k$ lie in `ssJSet q k`, that is: every elliptic Weierstrass curve $W$ over $k$ with $W.j = a$ has no nonzero affine point killed by $q$; assume further $a \ne 0$ and $a \ne 1728$. Inside the intermediate field `modularFunctionFieldBar (1 * q)` — the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-subfield of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}})$ generated by the coefficientwise image of `modularFunctionFieldFull (1 * q)` — put $G = j_{q} - j^{q}$, where $j$ is the series `jq` $= t^{-1}\cdot j_{\mathrm{Num}}$ and $j_{q}$ is its image under `qExpand ℚ (1 * q)`, the exponent rescaling $t \mapsto t^{q}$. Then the two Laurent series $q\cdot G^{-1}$ and `frickeInvolutionBar (1 * q)` applied to $G$ both lie in `CharPReduction.modularLocalized (1 * q) A.toSubring red` — the localisation of the subring of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}})$ generated by the constant series from $A$ together with `jqModC` and `jqNModC (1 * q)`, at the prime ideal of series with vanishing coefficientwise reduction — and each has nonzero image under `CharPReduction.modularRedLocHom (1 * q) A.toSubring red`.
--
--   This records the local structure of $X_0(q)$ at a width-one supersingular point in characteristic $q$ (Deligne–Rapoport): the node coordinate $G = j_q - j^q$ has Gauss valuation exactly $v(q)$ along the component of the special fibre through the cusp $\infty$, so that $q/G$ and its Fricke image are Gauss units there. It feeds the two-branch normalisation statements and the slope law for the opposite annulus of the $\infty$-chart.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_NodeLocalized_gaussData_nodeCoord.lean

